From: Pyra kernel work <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: ti: aess: open the McPDM back-end ports

With 0021 the PCM runs: MultiMedia1 LP opens, hw_params is accepted, the
stream reaches RUNNING and hw_ptr advances at 48156 frames a second. The DSP
processes it -- the DL1 buffer in SMEM carries changing sample data -- McPDM
is clocked and transmitting with exactly the DL1 pair enabled
(CTRL 0x4018 = WD_EN | bits 3,4), and no underflow is flagged.

And it is silent, because nothing puts anything in McPDM's FIFO. With the
port manager's debug on:

	port mm_dl_lp phy port 6 enabled
	aess 401f1000.aess: Port pdmdl1 is not open.
	McPDM-DL1: enable_be_port: mcpdm-abe-dl1 0

The front-end port enables. The back-end port does not, because it was never
opened, so omap_aess_port_enable() returns -EINVAL and
omap_aess_enable_data_transfer() never runs for PDM_DL. The AESS therefore
never starts pushing into the McPDM downlink FIFO, which stays zero while
McPDM faithfully transmits it.

omap_aess_dai_probe() opened every logical port except two:

	/* Skip McPDM DL1 and UL1 since they are handled differently */

Nothing in this tree handles them differently, or at all. Neither the built
machine driver nor the unbuilt copy in sound/soc/omap/ mentions them.

Opening them here is safe. omap_aess_port_open() touches no hardware: it
allocates the bookkeeping, marks the port PORT_DISABLED, adds it to a list and
makes some debugfs files. The hardware is only touched by
omap_aess_port_enable() from the back-end trigger, by which point DAPM has
powered the codec -- which is the ordering the original comment was presumably
protecting, and which opening a port does not disturb.

Verified to compile: `make sound/soc/ti/` exits 0 with 0013 through 0022 on a
pristine tree.

--- a/sound/soc/ti/aess/omap-aess-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/ti/aess/omap-aess-dai.c
@@ -1094,12 +1094,27 @@
 	int ret = 0;
 	int i;
 
+	/*
+	 * Every logical port, McPDM DL1 and UL1 included. They used to be
+	 * skipped here, with the note that they "are handled differently" --
+	 * and nothing in this tree handles them, so they were never opened at
+	 * all. The cost was silence with no error: the front-end port enables
+	 * on trigger, the DSP processes the stream, McPDM runs with the right
+	 * channels, and enable_be_port() then fails with
+	 *
+	 *	aess 401f1000.aess: Port pdmdl1 is not open.
+	 *
+	 * so omap_aess_enable_data_transfer() never runs for PDM_DL, the
+	 * AESS never pushes into McPDM's FIFO, and McPDM transmits zeroes.
+	 *
+	 * Opening a port here is safe because it touches no hardware:
+	 * omap_aess_port_open() allocates the bookkeeping, marks the port
+	 * PORT_DISABLED and adds it to a list. The hardware is only touched
+	 * by omap_aess_port_enable() from the back-end trigger, by which time
+	 * DAPM has powered the codec -- which is the ordering the original
+	 * comment was presumably protecting.
+	 */
 	for (i = 0; i < OMAP_AESS_LAST_LOGICAL_PORT_ID; i++) {
-		/* Skip McPDM DL1 and UL1 since they are handled differently */
-		if (i == OMAP_AESS_BE_PORT_PDM_DL1 ||
-		    i == OMAP_AESS_BE_PORT_PDM_UL1)
-			continue;
-
 		ret = omap_aess_port_open(aess, i);
 		if (ret)
 			goto err_port;
@@ -1108,14 +1123,8 @@
 	return 0;
 
 err_port:
-	for (--i; i >= 0; i--) {
-		/* Skip McPDM DL1 and UL1 since they are handled differently */
-		if (i == OMAP_AESS_BE_PORT_PDM_DL1 ||
-		    i == OMAP_AESS_BE_PORT_PDM_UL1)
-			continue;
-
+	for (--i; i >= 0; i--)
 		omap_aess_port_close(aess, i);
-	}
 
 	return ret;
 }
@@ -1125,14 +1134,8 @@
 	struct omap_aess *aess = snd_soc_dai_get_drvdata(dai);
 	int i;
 
-	for (i = 0; i < OMAP_AESS_LAST_LOGICAL_PORT_ID; i++) {
-		/* Skip McPDM DL1 and UL1 since they are handled differently */
-		if (i == OMAP_AESS_BE_PORT_PDM_DL1 ||
-		    i == OMAP_AESS_BE_PORT_PDM_UL1)
-			continue;
-
+	for (i = 0; i < OMAP_AESS_LAST_LOGICAL_PORT_ID; i++)
 		omap_aess_port_close(aess, i);
-	}
 
 	return 0;
 }
